---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, ENTITY, ENTITY_ADDRESS, ENTITY_FULL } from '../config';

const sections = [
  { id: 'agreement', title: 'This agreement' },
  { id: 'alpha', title: 'The alpha' },
  { id: 'what', title: 'What Tessera is and is not' },
  { id: 'decisions', title: 'Your orders and decisions' },
  { id: 'analyst', title: 'The analyst and your AI provider' },
  { id: 'connections', title: 'Brokers, prop firms and data' },
  { id: 'risk', title: 'Trading risk' },
  { id: 'licence', title: 'Your licence to use Tessera' },
  { id: 'content', title: 'Your content' },
  { id: 'fees', title: 'Fees' },
  { id: 'warranty', title: 'No warranty' },
  { id: 'liability', title: 'Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'indemnity', title: 'Indemnity' },
  { id: 'ending', title: 'Ending this agreement' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to these terms' },
  { id: 'law', title: 'Governing law and disputes' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The terms for using Tessera, a trading desk in a free, private, invite-only alpha: what it is and is not, your responsibility for your orders, the analyst, and the limits of our liability."
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="agreement">This agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and {ENTITY_FULL} ("Tessera", "we", "us") for your use of the Tessera
    desktop application, its runtime, this website and any related services (together, "Tessera"). By downloading,
    installing or using Tessera you accept these terms. The app also asks you to accept them the first time it opens,
    and again whenever they change. If you do not accept them, do not use Tessera.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains how we handle personal data, and the
    <a href="/risk">risk disclaimer</a> is part of these terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tessera is run by an individual entrepreneur registered in Georgia, not by a company or any other separate legal
    entity. "We" and "us" in these terms mean that individual entrepreneur.
  </p>
  <p>
    You must be at least 18 years old and able to enter a binding contract where you live. If you use Tessera for a
    company, you accept these terms for that company and confirm you may do so.
  </p>

  <h2 id="alpha">The alpha</h2>
  <p>
    Tessera is in a free, private, invite-only alpha. Only people we invite can use it, and your invitation and account
    are for you alone.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is unfinished software: features may change, break or be removed, data formats may change between versions, and
    the alpha may end. Use a paper account while you learn it, and keep another way to see and manage your positions,
    such as your broker's own platform.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what">What Tessera is and is not</h2>
  <p>
    Tessera is software. It displays market data from connections you set up, helps you research and journal, and sends
    the orders you place or approve to the broker or trading system you connect.
  </p>
  <p>
    You bring your own data and your own AI. Tessera does not sell or include market data, and it does not include an AI
    model: you connect your own broker or data vendor, and your own AI agent, each under your own account with them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tessera is <strong>not</strong> a broker, a futures commission merchant, an introducing broker, an exchange, a
    commodity trading advisor or an investment adviser. We do not hold your money, execute or clear your trades, or act
    on your behalf. Nothing in Tessera or on this website, including anything the analyst writes, is investment advice,
    a recommendation or an offer to buy or sell any financial instrument. Tessera does not know your circumstances and
    gives no financial, tax or legal advice.
  </p>

  <h2 id="decisions">Your orders and decisions</h2>
  <p>
    Every trading decision is yours. The analyst drafts orders; you approve them. A draft is not sent until you approve
    it in the app, unless you have switched that analyst session to Full access yourself. You are responsible for every
    order sent from Tessera on your accounts: the orders you place yourself, the drafts you approve, and any order the
    analyst places while you have given it Full access. You are responsible for checking each order's instrument, side,
    size, price, type and bracket before you send or approve it, and for the result.
  </p>
  <p>
    Risk limits, hotkeys, brackets, breakeven, the trade copier and alerts are tools you configure. They can fail, act
    later than you expect or behave differently from what you intended, for example when a connection drops or a fill
    differs between accounts. Do not rely on them as your only protection.
  </p>

  <h2 id="analyst">The analyst and your AI provider</h2>
  <p>
    The analyst runs on an AI agent you provide, such as Claude Code or Codex, signed in to your own account with that
    provider. Your use of that agent is governed by your agreement with its provider, including its fees, limits and
    data terms. We are not responsible for the provider's service, availability or handling of your data.
  </p>
  <p>
    AI output can be wrong, incomplete or out of date, and it can misread charts, levels or data. Treat what the analyst
    says as a draft for your judgment. Every order it prepares is a draft that waits for your approval, in every mode
    but one: if you switch a session to Full access, the analyst can place, change and close orders on your accounts
    without asking, including live accounts. That mode is never on unless you turn it on, and when you do you accept the
    risk of it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="connections">Brokers, prop firms and data</h2>
  <p>
    You connect your own brokers, prop-firm accounts, market-data and level vendors. Their terms, fees, rules and
    exchange data agreements apply to you, and you are responsible for meeting them, including any rules of an
    evaluation or funded account and your professional or non-professional data status. Market data may be delayed,
    incomplete or wrong. Demo data in Tessera is simulated and does not reflect any real market.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your connection credentials are stored on your computer, in your operating system's keychain. You are responsible
    for keeping your computer and your accounts secure.
  </p>

  <h2 id="risk">Trading risk</h2>
  <p>
    Trading futures and other leveraged instruments carries substantial risk of loss, and you can lose more than you
    deposited. Past results, whether real, simulated or from a backtest, do not predict future results. Read the
    <a href="/risk">risk disclaimer</a> before you trade with Tessera; you accept those risks by using it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="licence">Your licence to use Tessera</h2>
  <p>
    Tessera is open source under the
    <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0">Apache License, Version 2.0</a>. That licence, not these
    terms, sets what you may do with Tessera's code and the builds made from it: use, copy, change and redistribute them
    under its conditions. These terms cover your use of Tessera and of the services we run for it. You may not use
    Tessera to break the law or the terms of a broker, exchange or data vendor, or interfere with the security of our
    services. The Tessera name and logo remain ours. Third-party components and marks, Rithmic's among them, are
    licensed under their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="content">Your content</h2>
  <p>
    Your journal, notes, layouts, indicators, research and conversations are yours. They are kept on your computer. If
    we later offer an optional cloud account to sync them, its terms will be added here before it launches, and it will
    never sync your credentials.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fees">Fees</h2>
  <p>
    The alpha is free of charge. If we introduce paid plans, we will publish their prices and terms before charging you
    anything. Fees charged by your broker, data vendors, prop firm or AI provider are between you and them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="warranty">No warranty</h2>
  <p class="caps">
    Tessera is provided "as is" and "as available". To the fullest extent the law allows, we disclaim all warranties,
    express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy and non-infringement. We
    do not warrant that Tessera will be uninterrupted, timely, secure or free of errors, that data shown in it is
    accurate, or that any order will be sent, accepted or filled as you intend.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p class="caps">
    To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any trading losses, lost profits, missed trades,
    slippage, or indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages arising from your use of Tessera, including
    losses caused by software errors, connection failures, data errors, the behaviour of an AI agent, or the actions of
    a broker, exchange or vendor. Our total liability for any claim relating to Tessera is limited to the greater of the
    amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim and EUR 100. During the free alpha you pay us nothing, so
    the limit is EUR 100.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, such as liability for fraud, gross negligence
    or wilful misconduct or, where applicable, death or personal injury caused by negligence. If you are a consumer,
    these terms do not take away any right that the law of the country where you live gives you and that a contract
    cannot exclude.
  </p>

  <h2 id="indemnity">Indemnity</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, you agree to indemnify us against claims by third parties arising from your trading,
    your breach of these terms, or your breach of the terms of a broker, prop firm, exchange or vendor.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ending">Ending this agreement</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using Tessera at any time by uninstalling it. We may suspend or end your licence if you breach these
    terms or if we end the alpha. The sections on your orders, the analyst, no warranty, limitation of liability,
    indemnity and governing law survive the end of this agreement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. We will post the new version here with its date, and the app will show you the new
    version and ask you to accept it before you go on using Tessera. If you do not accept it, stop using Tessera.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of Georgia (the country), and disputes will be resolved by the courts of
    Tbilisi, Georgia, except where the law where you live gives you the right to bring a claim locally.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, or by post to {ENTITY},{' '}
    {ENTITY_ADDRESS}.
  </p>
</Legal>
